cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PCAPro: an offline, browser-based platform for guided principal component analysis"
abstract: >-
  PCAPro is a self-contained web application that performs a complete principal component
  analysis entirely in the browser, with no installation and no server-side computation. It
  covers data preparation, verification of assumptions, extraction with eight retention
  criteria, seven rotations, factor maps, interpretation and a publication-ready report.
  Since version 1.1.0 it also performs correspondence analysis, multiple correspondence
  analysis, factor analysis of mixed data and multiple factor analysis on a shared
  generalized-SVD core, recommends which of them fits the data at hand, and clusters the
  individuals hierarchically on the factor coordinates. The interface, the embedded
  methodological guidance and the report are bilingual (Spanish and English).
